Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:43:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] IMPORTS-6: undoing a merge, or the import behind it, reverses
 the merge

Undoing a Review merge from Activity restored the transaction but left
the imported row 'merged' into it: the bank's row was in neither the
ledger nor Review. It now returns to Review, as an undone approval's does.

Undoing a batch removed only what it created; a row of it merged into a
transaction already in the ledger left that transaction cleared and
carrying the undone statement's narration ("removed 0"). The merge's
columns are now put back from its event, unless the transaction changed
since, when it is left and listed with the edited records (IL2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
